GitHub Issue:
Post Date: 2016-09-19T15:47:48Z
Current Date: April 4 2025
Title: Changing the name of an association to get output as JSON
Description: ## What you are doing?

So, lets say I have an association (below) and it has been included and then output to JSON.

``` js
// in the model
User.belongsToMany(models.Permissions, {through: models.UsersPermissions, foreignKey: 'userId'});

// included
db.Users.findAll({ 
        include: [ {
            model: db.Permissions,
        through: {
                 attributes: []
                }
        }]
})

//output
"Permissions": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "name": "add-role",
          "description": "Allows the user to add a new role to the system"
        }
      ]
```
## What do you expect to happen?

Now, that final output comes out as a 'Permission', note the capital P.

What I would expect is a lower case 'p', because I don;t know of any standard that would like that capitalized.

The only way to change this is to use the "as" operator. Therefore...

``` js
// in the model
User.belongsToMany(models.Permissions, {through: models.UsersPermissions, foreignKey: 'userId', as: 'permissions'});

// included
db.Users.findAll({ 
        include: [ {
        model: db.Permissions,
                as: 'permissions',
        through: {
                 attributes: []
                }
        }]
})

//output
"permissions": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "name": "add-role",
          "description": "Allows the user to add a new role to the system"
        }
      ]
```

Now, you may feel this is great, what isnt great however is that this "as" operator must be used in both the model AND the includes.

Is this the only way to have this happen? Or have I got something wrong here?


